  "language": "en",
  "text": "ordinarium.praefatio-defunctorum",
  "about": "The Preface for the Dead. It proclaims the hope of resurrection and confesses that the life of the faithful is changed, not ended, and that an eternal home in heaven awaits after the earthly dwelling.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "narrative": "Then the priest separates his hands and holds them apart until the end of the Preface. When it is finished, he joins them again and, bowing, says: Sanctus." },
    "s02": { "translation": "It is truly meet and just, right and profitable for salvation, that we should at all times and in all places give thanks unto Thee:" },
    "s03": { "translation": "O Lord, holy Father, almighty eternal God: through Christ our Lord." },
    "s04": { "translation": "In Whom the hope of a blessed resurrection hath shone forth for us, so that those whom the certain lot of dying saddens may be consoled by the promise of future immortality." },
    "s05": { "translation": "For to Thy faithful, O Lord, life is changed, not taken away; and when the house of this earthly sojourn is dissolved, an eternal dwelling is prepared in heaven." },
    "s06": { "translation": "And therefore with Angels and Archangels, with Thrones and Dominions, and with all the hosts of the heavenly army, we sing the hymn of Thy glory, evermore saying:" }
  },
